Votum is a decision model fine-tuned from swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-8B (Apertus 1.5, Swiss AI Initiative). The base model is
distributed under the Apache License 2.0 and the Apertus Acceptable Use Policy v1.5
(https://github.com/swiss-ai/apertus-legal/blob/main/apertus_1.5/USAGE_POLICY.pdf); anyone who uses or redistributes Votum
with the base model is bound by that policy. Votum is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Swiss AI Initiative,
EPFL, ETH Zurich or CSCS.

This software contains code derived from the following projects:

- jeff-serve (https://github.com/j-geuter/Jeff, formerly j-geuter/jeff-serve), Apache License 2.0.
  Copyright 2026 Jonathan Geuter, Andrew Cheng, David Alvarez-Melis.
  src/votum/request.py converts TypeSafe questions to options the way jeff's typesafe.py does (which follows
  JevBench's semif_direct adapter, https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench, MIT License).
- Apertus 1.5 image tokenizer, Apache License 2.0: src/votum/vision.py is a standalone copy of the image tokenizer's
  encoder and image processor from the Swiss AI Initiative's transformers (Apertus1p5VisionTokenizerModel,
  Apertus1p5ImageProcessor; https://github.com/swiss-ai/transformers).

